;;; v3/kernel/loader.shard — the loader.
;;; A package root and its files: each file is a module
;;; named by its path from the root; `import` loads a file once (a cycle is
;;; refused) and makes the imported module's closure visible, opening
;;; nothing; every module sees Lean's Init — every
;;; declaration of the pinned export, of which the ones the module needs are
;;; loaded on demand from the export's index (initload.shard), the meta
;;; line checked against the pin; `use` opens a prefix for the rest of
;;; the file; `trusts` widens the file's assumption policy; every declared
;;; form goes through the reader (reader.shard) into K's raw entry
;;; (k/add.shard `check`, which ingests), and an admitted declaration's
;;; axiom closure (k/axioms.shard) is checked against the file's policy —
;;; outside it, the declaration is reported and dropped, the environment
;;; kept as it was. What the loader records per declaration is the
;;; acceptance record (the driver load.shard prints it): the
;;; identity (K name and content fingerprint), the module, the axiom
;;; closure, and the environment revision (the visible
;;; modules and their hashes on their MODULE lines). Nothing here is
;;; authority: K's verdicts are K's.

